 "po_digest_md": "**Luz Amanhã, 05.11, evening**\n\n**What happened:** The posts on 05.11 went out on time with dated links (T-0055, T-0056) and on X (T-0032). Accepted: per-day Open Graph previews (T-0054), new columns in the /d/ archive (T-0060) and `missing_reason` in the JSON (T-0061). People today: 5 in total, 2 engaged; both engaged visitors came from the X post. Telegram and Bluesky brought no people (the Bluesky hits were preview bots).\n\n**Decisions:**\n- X looks promising, but there are only 2 people so far. We do not add posts. The planned EN-first X post on 08.11 (T-0040) is the second test, and the channels will be compared by `?src=` on 10.11.\n- G3 cannot be read from the logs. The analyst will record the subscriber count from the public channel page and split the /go/telegram/ clicks by visitor type.\n- The developer will add one line next to the Telegram link: what you get and when (07:00 and about 14:00 Lisbon time), PT+EN. This is a persona wish and serves G3.\n- From 10.11 the marketer writes the plan for the next week.\n- The python-requests spike on 04.11 is already explained (T-0052).\n\n**Waiting for the owner:** Can ops record the channel's subscriber count in metrics.json once a day? Still pending from before: the channel avatar and rotating the GitHub token (after 11.11).\n\n**Spend:** $4.06 of $20.",
